# Firebrand Agents workflow

Use the shared **docs/ contract** in the application repo. Prefer existing files; create `docs/` from Firebrand Agents templates when missing.

| Artifact | Path | Owner |
|----------|------|-------|
| Plan | `docs/project-plan.md` | PM |
| Analysis | `docs/analysis.md` | BA |
| UI/UX | `docs/uiux-design.md` | UID |
| Tech design | `docs/technical-design.md` | TL |
| Data | `docs/data-design.md` | DBE |
| DevOps | `docs/devops.md` | DO |
| Test strategy | `docs/test-strategy.md` | QAL |
| Test report (web) | `docs/test-report.md` | playwright-tester |
| Test report (Flutter) | `docs/flutter-test-report.md` | flutter-tester |
| Security review | `docs/security-review.md` | SEC |

Stable IDs: `FR-`, `NFR-`, `SCR-`, `WP-`, `T-`, `Q-`. Do not silently rewrite BA FRs.

**Only PM** (`project-manager`) asks the client. Other roles list **Blockers for PM** and mark guesses **Assumption (pending PM)**. Never invent business rules or FRs.

Default stacks: **ASP.NET Core / C#**, **Angular**, **Flutter**. Match the repo when it already differs. Playwright is **web-only**. Native Flutter tests are `flutter-tester`.

Default order: PM → BA → UID+TL → DBE → BED+DO → FED/MFD → QAL → playwright-tester and/or flutter-tester → L10N (if multi-language) → A11Y → SEC+CR → TL → TW. Invoke PERF when NFRs require it. One work package per developer invoke; do not build the whole product in one pass.

If `.cursor/rules/project-context.mdc` exists, read it for source control, CI, hosting, auth, stack overrides, and locales. Do not re-ask the user for info already in that file.

**Always use the pre-built named subagents** (`business-analyst`, `team-lead`, `uiux-designer`, `database-engineer`, `backend-developer`, `frontend-developer`, `mobile-flutter-developer`, `devops-engineer`, `qa-lead`, `playwright-tester`, `flutter-tester`, `accessibility-specialist`, `security-reviewer`, `code-reviewer`, `performance-engineer`, `technical-writer`, `localization-engineer`). Never create ad-hoc agents with custom system prompts. Never role-play as another specialist. Invoke subagents by name or output a handoff prompt for the user.

Subagents have clean context — invoke with full paths and FR/WP/SCR IDs.
